# Purpose

This document defines the source control engineering standards for the hubIO platform.

Its purpose is to establish consistent principles for managing source code, preserving engineering history, and enabling safe collaboration while supporting long-term product evolution.

---

# Scope

This standard defines:

* Source control philosophy
* Repository integrity
* Change management
* Collaboration principles
* Source control governance
* Repository evolution

It intentionally excludes Git commands, branching workflows, repository hosting platforms, merge strategies, and implementation-specific version control techniques, which are defined by their respective Engineering Standards.

---

# Constitutional Interpretation

This document extends the hubIO Engineering Constitution.

It applies constitutional engineering principles to source control, ensuring every change contributes to a reliable, understandable, and maintainable engineering history.

